   "id": "defence",
   "title": "Planetary defence",
   "duration_s": 30,
   "narration": [
    "And they can look where ground telescopes cannot. Here, a fifty-metre asteroid approaches from the direction of the Sun, invisible from the ground. FACET's search finds it, thirty telescopes lock on, and within the hour we know it will hit, and where, with hours to spare. Hours of warning cannot stop an asteroid; they can save lives."
   ],
